    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "// Get all rows from Google Sheets\nconst rows = $input.all();\n\n// Find highest version\nlet latestVersion = 0;\n\nfor (const row of rows) {\n  const version = Number(row.json.Version || 0);\n\n  if (version > latestVersion) {\n    latestVersion = version;\n  }\n}\n\n// Get Jira issue details\nconst issue = $('Get an issue').first().json;\n\nreturn [{\n  json: {\n    ...issue,\n    nextVersion: latestVersion + 1\n  }\n}];"
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        672,
        -192
      ],
      "id": "4b3ff1cf-8b68-46d2-8544-cb421b3093ed",
      "name": "Prepare Next Version"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=You are a Senior QA Test Engineer.\n\nYour task is to generate comprehensive manual test cases from the Jira User Story provided below.\n\nJira Story ID:\n{{ $json.key }}\n\nProject:\n{{ $json.fields.project.name }}\n\nEpic:\n{{ $json.fields.parent.fields.summary }}\n\nUser Story Summary:\n{{ $json.fields.summary }}\n\nUser Story Description:\n{{ $json.fields.description }}\n\nInstructions:\n\nGenerate comprehensive manual test cases covering:\n\n- Positive Testing\n- Negative Testing\n- Boundary Value Testing\n- Validation Testing\n- UI Testing\n- Security Testing\n- Accessibility Testing\n\nGenerate at least 15 test cases.\n\nReturn ONLY a valid JSON array.\n\nFor every generated test case, populate the following fields using the Jira story provided:\n\n- Story ID = Jira Story ID\n- Epic = Epic name\n- Feature = Functional feature/module inferred from the User Story\n- User Story Summary = Jira User Story Summary\n\nThese four values must be repeated in every JSON object.\n\nEach JSON object must contain exactly these fields:\n\n{\n\"Story ID\": \"\",\n\"Epic\": \"\",\n\"Feature\": \"\",\n\"User Story Summary\": \"\",\n\"Test Case ID\": \"\",\n\"Test Scenario\": \"\",\n\"Test Objective\": \"\",\n\"Preconditions\": \"\",\n\"Test Steps\": \"\",\n\"Test Data\": \"\",\n\"Expected Result\": \"\",\n\"Test Type\": \"\",\n\"Priority\": \"\"\n}\n\nRules:\n\n1. Test Case ID should start from TC001.\n2. Test Steps must be numbered.\n3. Priority must be High, Medium or Low.\n4. Test Type must be one of:\n   Positive\n   Negative\n   Boundary\n   Validation\n   UI\n   Security\n   Accessibility\n5. Return ONLY JSON.\n6. Do not include explanations.\n7. Do not include Markdown.\n8. Do not include code fences.\n\nIMPORTANT:\n\nReturn STRICTLY VALID JSON.\n\nDo not escape single quotes using \\'.\n\nSingle quotes may appear normally.\n\nEscape only double quotes according to JSON syntax.\n\nYour response must be directly parseable by JSON.parse().",
        "batching": {}
      },
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.chainLlm",
      "typeVersion": 1.9,
      "position": [
        896,
        -192
      ],
      "id": "46472db6-d2f5-4984-ac45-cc15d670692d",
      "name": "Basic LLM Chain"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "const aiText = $input.first().json.text;\n\n// Remove invalid escaped single quotes that Gemini may generate\nconst cleaned = aiText.replace(/\\\\'/g, \"'\");\n\nconst testCases = JSON.parse(cleaned);\n\n// Generate current date & time\nconst generationDate = new Date().toISOString();\n\nreturn testCases.map(tc => {\n\n  // Permanent unique identifier\n  tc[\"Unique Test Case Key\"] =\n    `${tc[\"Story ID\"]}_${tc[\"Test Case ID\"]}`;\n\n  // Workflow metadata\n  tc[\"Generated By\"] = \"WF01 - AI Test Case Generator\";\n  tc[\"AI Model\"] = \"Gemini 3.5 Flash\";\n  tc[\"Prompt Version\"] = \"v1.0\";\n  tc[\"Generation Date\"] = generationDate;\n  tc[\"Comments\"] = \"\";\n\n  // Versioning\n  tc[\"Version\"] = $('Prepare Next Version').first().json.nextVersion;\n  tc[\"Status\"] = \"Draft\";\n\n  return {\n    json: tc\n  };\n});"
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
